      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A metal-lustrous self-standing film, named \"porphyrin foil\", was formed from a glass-forming polymeric porphyrin. The amorphous glass nature of the porphyrin foil played a key role in spontaneously producing a smooth surface. Its sharp contrast in intense absorption and specular reflection of light at each wavelength provided a brilliant metallic lustre."},
